# `number` Standalone Wire Specification

`number` uses Xahau's `Number` decimal representation and serializes its
normalized signed mantissa and exponent as a fixed 12-byte payload:

| Bytes | Component | Encoding |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 0..7 | `mantissa` | Signed 64-bit integer, big-endian two's-complement bits. |
| 8..11 | `exponent` | Signed 32-bit integer, big-endian two's-complement bits. |

There is no outer field header. Decode requires exactly 12 bytes. Zero uses
`Number`'s canonical zero state; nonzero values normalize to a 16-digit
mantissa with exponent range -32768 through +32768.

The CLI accepts a JSON string or integer. Its decimal grammar rejects leading
zeroes (except `0`), incomplete fractions/exponents, and non-decimal values.
Arbitrary-length significant input is reduced directly to 16 digits with one
round-to-nearest-even step. The guard digit and every later sticky digit
participate, avoiding both silent tail loss and double rounding.

